Title: Booking reminders that ask the patient to reply
Filing date: 2 March 2022
Priority: SYN-PRI-2021-0303, 3 March 2021
Publication date: 15 September 2022
Status: Application published

Abstract
A scheduling system sends a booking reminder some hours ahead of an appointment, asking the
patient to reply. If no reply arrives within a set number of hours after the reminder, the
appointment is marked as at risk so that staff can follow it up.

Claims
1. A method comprising sending a booking reminder hours ahead of an appointment and asking the patient to reply; and, when no reply arrives within a reply period after the reminder, marking the appointment as at risk.
2. The method of claim 1, wherein the reply period is between 4 and 12 hours.
